# November 19, 2026: eastern and middle Washington County, New York: Salem, Cambridge, White Creek, Hartford, Granville
# (South and Middle Granville), Easton, Greenwich, Hebron, Fort Miller and Whitehall's Main Street. Drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py --state ny (region wash, 27 places, nearly all along the Hudson and the old Champlain Canal; the
# country east of it had only covered bridges and the Susan B. Anthony house). Almost all standing buildings: old
# village centres, churches and meeting houses, two museums, an opera house, a tavern and an armory. Sources opened in
# this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), HMdb marker pages, and through tools/page.py the Town of
# Salem's landmark tour and cemetery pages, the Lakes to Locks Passage page for the Salem courthouse, the Pomeroy
# Foundation's courthouse marker page, Hubbard Hall's visit and history pages, the Town of Hartford's museum page, the
# Slate Valley Museum's visit page, the Lakes to Locks Passage page for the museum, the Easton Library's Quaker history,
# New York Yearly Meeting's page for Easton Friends and the state military museum's Whitehall Armory page.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
def L(t,u): return [t,u]
def HM(n,t): return L('HMdb: '+t,'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=%d'%n)
